    <statement><p>Sketch the region of integration for the following integral.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle \int_{0}^{\pi/4} \int_{0}^{6 / \cos(\theta)} f(r,\theta) \, r \, dr \, d\theta</m></p>
<p>The region of integration is bounded by</p>
<p><var form="buttons">
<li>
<p><m>y = 0, y = x, \mbox{ and } y = 6</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>y = 0, y = x, \mbox{ and } x = 6</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>y = 0, y = \sqrt{36 - x^2}, \mbox{ and } x = 6</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>y = 0, x = \sqrt{36 - y^2}, \mbox{ and } y = 6</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p>None of the above</p>
</li>
</var></p>
</statement>
